        "spans": [
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 16,
            "end": 585,
            "text": "I’ve only recently started working with n8n and I’m currently working on a workflow for automatic email sorting. I’m having a problem with my Code Node and the subsequent IF Node. My Code Node apparently doesn’t reliably recognize emails that contain certain text. Additionally, the IF Node doesn’t output the Boolean value (true or false) as expected, so the emails aren’t being sorted correctly. Unfortunately, I haven’t been able to find the cause so far. Does anyone have experience with this problem and can give me a tip on how to configure my workflow correctly?",
            "sha256": "9d2a54bda6ae33f3bc3221fd67c2b44dcb173ee3c9d2cc25b2eb63fa1d6fa31e"
          },
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 682,
            "end": 717,
            "text": "What is the error message (if any)?",
            "sha256": "4fa361830b71f510b256316235f5b3bdd466731ffe67d770ab92ad39a8ceb398"
          },
          {
            "kind": "context",
            "start": 718,
            "end": 744,
            "text": "Please share your workflow",
            "sha256": "f6d07f3f5ec993a866ee41521c65984d8b24405de0d151ea66345a4d9284165a"
          },
          {
            "kind": "context",
